From d64a48125f782742e788e16471feb150f72f70a8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mikekinney@Mikes-MacBook-Pro.local>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 15:29:29 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(post): an explicit M5 after a probe's tool change in
 every post

A probe section relied on the control's tool change to stop the
spindle. Every mill post (fanuc, haas, tormach, sinumerik, heidenhain,
mazak) now writes its spindle-stop word - M5, MOTOFF on Mazak - after
the tool change and length offset, before coolant and the first move,
when the section states a spindle speed of 0 (only a probe does; tools
refuse rpm 0). A cutting section and a legacy stream with no
SpindleSpeed PARAM post byte-identical.

Goldens: one added "M5" line after G43 in the four Fanuc probe goldens
(probe_bore_centre, probe_corner, probe_corner_negative,
probe_edge_negative_x) and tormach/probe_guard_moves.

Pinned by probe_spindle_stop::{a_probe_section_stops_its_spindle_after_the_tool_change_on_every_mill_post,
a_cutting_section_states_no_spindle_stop_before_its_first_move}.

Fixes #574

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAgjpiZbXSvmXLvdmL
